   "source": [
    "# HARey constellation cards\n",
    "\n",
    "__HARey__ (pen name of Hans Augusto Reyersbach) was an illustrator and author. He took an interest in astronomy and wrote the books _The Stars: A New Way to see them_  and _Find the constellations_ to teach children about stargazing. In them he tried to redrawn the constellations diagrams to be more similar to the objects they are named after, instead of the abstract shapes used in modern astronomy.  \n",
    "\n",
    "This project is my personal homage to HARey's work, and it borrows his idea of making learning the constellations a challenge by creating a Memory-like game to recognize the constellations without the lines."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "from matplotlib.font_manager import FontProperties\n",
    "from datetime import datetime\n",
    "import pytz\n",
    "import pandas as pd"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## The project base\n",
    "This project borrows a lot from __Stellarium__, an open source planetary software. In the _Sky Culture_ section users can see different constellations shapes created by different cultures, and among them there are HARey's drawings. The _index.json_ file provides the constellation lines data and asterisms and the Hipparcos catalogues provides the stars positions to draw the constellations."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from HARey.astro_projection import Observer, stereo_centered\n",
    "from HARey.loader import load_constellations, load_stars"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The __constellations__ dictionary contains each constellations lines and stars. The key is an abbreviation of the constellation name (e.g., Ori for Orion). Constellations with keys like __.Orib__ are a subgroup of stars that are assigned a name by HARey (e.g. .Orib is Orion's belt). The __main_ids__ list contains the ids of the 88 IAU constellations."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "['UMi', 'Dra', 'Cas', 'Cep', 'Cam', 'UMa', 'Leo', 'CVn', 'LMi', 'Boo']\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "#Load the constellations  \n",
    "constellations, main_ids, asterisms, helpers, named_stars = load_constellations()\n",
    "# Load the stars positions and the constellations they belong to\n",
    "stars = load_stars()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Print the first 10 ids as an example\n",
    "print(main_ids[0:10])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The stars are projected using a __stereographic__ projection, which is a projection from spherical surface to plane which conserves the angles at which lines meet, locally preserving the shapes (further from the center, the stretching distorts the overall diagram). The center of the projection is the brightest star of each constellation."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "stars = stars[stars['magnitude'] < 5]\n",
    "local_stars = stars.loc[constellations['UMa']['stars']]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Take the brightest star of the constellation as the ccenter (zenith) of the projection\n",
    "brightest_star = local_stars.iloc[np.argmin(local_stars['magnitude'])]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Perform the stereographic projection\n",
    "stars_x, stars_y = stereo_centered(stars['ra'], stars['dec'], brightest_star['ra'], brightest_star['dec'])\n",
    "\n",
    "# Convert the values to  Pandas series by adding the index\n",
    "stars_x = pd.Series(data = stars_x, index=stars.index)\n",
    "stars_y = pd.Series(data = stars_y, index=stars.index)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 5,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
